cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Mera.jl in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Mera.jl: Fast, conservation-correct, code-agnostic analysis of astrophysical simulations in Julia"
abstract: >-
  Mera.jl is a Julia package for reading and analysing astrophysical simulation output. RAMSES
  adaptive-mesh-refinement data (hydro, gravity, particles, clumps, radiative transfer) is the
  native format; self-registering readers also load PLUTO, Chombo, Athena++, FLASH and the
  GADGET/GIZMO/AREPO/SWIFT HDF5 particle family (including gas-cell physics, cosmological unit
  conversion and multi-file snapshots), and the code-agnostic analysis layer runs on all of them
  unchanged. It provides spatial selection, a derived-quantity registry with physical units,
  weighted profiles and phase diagrams, mass-conserving projections (axis-aligned and off-axis)
  and covering grids, a pluggable structure (clump/halo) finder, and a conservation-correct
  inflow/outflow flux-budget tool, all checked by a data-free correctness oracle.
type: software
